{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people","id":1560092,"title":"Beating Common Sense Into People?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-19T05:46:25-07:00","id":1560092,"title":"Beating Common Sense Into People?","content":"Okay, so if the Akashic Brotherhood are known for their magical kung fu, and their pursuit of enlightenment, then why have none of them invented a spell that allows them to quite literally beat knowledge into their skulls?<br /> <br /> It seems like a more expedient solution than trying to reeducate the subject through more 'conventional' methods.<br /> <br /> Plus, we know that the Technocracy already has some kind of process that works along a similar idea. Where they physically and psychologically torture you, until you adopt their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T07:35:59-07:00","id":1560093,"title":"","content":"They likely have. I'm sure there there are Akashic rotes that teach through sparring and grueling training sessions. But that's for willing students, it's not going to work as well if the 'student' isn't playing along. Keep in mind that the Traditions have been working together for so long that not many members want to force their paradigm on someone at the barrel of a gun. For those who do, it's possible, but there's not likely a widespread set of rotes for it.<br /> <br /> There's also another limit. Knowledge is not the same thing as understanding or enlightenment, and the latter is what the Akashics want their students to gain. To go any further than the fundamentals the Akashics would have to believe Enlightenment could be imparted, believe it could be imparted that way, and be able to render said Enlightenment down into coherent packets that could be imparted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T08:54:16-07:00","id":1560094,"title":"","content":"Ascension is a process, not a pill you can give someone. Having said that, Do is the path and repetitive chanting or training is the beat down that wears the stones on that path. Be patient, Grasshopper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T09:33:51-07:00","id":1560097,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the training it's part of the deal. Sweat and tears, the companionship, the teacher-student relationship ... are all part of the process that make a better kung-fu.<br /> <br /> <i>Of course</i> the Syndicate would want you to skip the training and just get the results - oh, but don't tell them about an &quot;universal income&quot; because how are you so lazy that you don't want to work for your bread. Scarcity it's a foundation, we can't just solve it with science!.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T10:21:30-07:00","id":1560098,"title":"","content":"Not that I don't feel you on this. I had a magic intelligence stick when I was younger. It did make people stop saying foolish things, but only until they woke up. After that they were usually worse. Magic is complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12269-heilong","name":"Heilong","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T14:10:55-07:00","id":1560099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heilong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1560098#post1560098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I don't feel you on this. I had a magic intelligence stick when I was younger. It did make people stop saying foolish things, but only until they woke up. After that they were usually worse. Magic is complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Come on, I saw the zoo keepers hand feeding the tigers an hour ago. I'll just climb in, snap a quick selfie and get out!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>*Thwack!*</b><br /> <br /> &quot;On second thought, maybe I shouldn't do that...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 05-19-2026, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T14:46:10-07:00","id":1560101,"title":"","content":"In one of the editions of Mage, <b><i>Pass for Normal </i></b>was given as an example of a <b>Etherian </b>rote. As one effect of the spell was to temporarily induce <b>Common Sense </b>into the target of the rote, a Mage with a talisman with this rote would be a major superhero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T14:57:50-07:00","id":1560102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1560093#post1560093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also another limit. Knowledge is not the same thing as understanding or enlightenment, and the latter is what the Akashics want their students to gain. To go any further than the fundamentals the Akashics would have to believe Enlightenment could be imparted, believe it could be imparted that way, and be able to render said Enlightenment down into coherent packets that could be imparted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We call it the <i>&quot;Paradigm of Fafo.&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> First cultivated by Arch Mage Fafo.<br /> <br /> It is said that he never had to fight the same enemy twice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 05-19-2026, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T14:55:45-07:00","id":1561174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1560093#post1560093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also another limit. Knowledge is not the same thing as understanding or enlightenment, and the latter is what the Akashics want their students to gain. To go any further than the fundamentals the Akashics would have to believe Enlightenment could be imparted, believe it could be imparted that way, and be able to render said Enlightenment down into coherent packets that could be imparted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, there's lots of stories about masters who believe in the concept of <i>&quot;teaching through pain&quot;</i> - so yeah, this could actually work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T16:16:22-07:00","id":1561259,"title":"","content":"You're thinking of St Cuthbert. <br /> <br /> From Greyhawk.<br /> <br /> 'of the Cudgel'. He hits you over the head with it <br /> <br /> The Akashics don't believe in common sense they run on walls and fight gun men hand to hand. Hand to gun. Sometimes they use guns too though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T20:40:40-07:00","id":1561267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561259#post1561259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking of St Cuthbert.<br /> <br /> From Greyhawk.<br /> <br /> 'of the Cudgel'. He hits you over the head with it<br /> <br /> The Akashics don't believe in common sense they run on walls and fight gun men hand to hand. Hand to gun. Sometimes they use guns too though.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Fun Fact:</b> historically, Ninjas used any weapon they could get their hands on, <b>including flintlock rifles.</b><br /> <br /> This is because the image of the honorable and chivalrous samurai is mostly bullshit. They were ruthless thugs, and the first ninja were peasants rebelling against their tyrannical oppression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T05:01:02-07:00","id":1561289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561267#post1561267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Fun Fact:</b> historically, Ninjas used any weapon they could get their hands on, <b>including flintlock rifles.</b><br /> <br /> This is because the image of the honorable and chivalrous samurai is mostly bullshit. They were ruthless thugs, and the first ninja were peasants rebelling against their tyrannical oppression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additional note on Ninjas. In the period were the myth of the Ninja got formalized two factors beyond stage conventions made it easy for those seeking revenge on Samurai to get close to their targets. First there was an aristocratic custom of NOT looking at the faces of servants and inferiors. It was an additude of proclaiming others to unimportant to bother with. Thus even a well known enemy might with patience get near to a Samurai and wait for a chance to strike. Second, period Samurai tended not to allow much if any organization among servants and retainers. It was entirely possible for servants employed in the same household not to know or even be aware of the existence of other employees. As bizarre as those two customs sound there is plenty of evidence for both customs in the 17th century. <br /> <br /> Thus, a person wanting revenge on a Samurai could simply go to their residence, walk in and start doing housework like they belonged there. One person claimed to have done that and claimed evidence that she had been paid under two different names! Since Samurai didn't look at servants or even acknowledge their presence unless they wanted something there were always multiple chances to get physically close to a Samurai. Thus someone who wanted to kill a Samurai just had to be patient and wait for an opportunity. <br /> <br /> The myth of the terrifying Ninja super assassins was a way for Samurai to explain why they hadn't seen someone hiding in plain sight. In order not to look like idiot snobs the Samurai created a myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:48:30-07:00","id":1561311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561289#post1561289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The myth of the terrifying Ninja super assassins was a way for Samurai to explain why they hadn't seen someone hiding in plain sight. In order not to look like idiot snobs the Samurai created a myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it worked.<br /> <br /> First, Samurai didn't look servants in the eye, which is not the same as not recognizing them despite not staring the face directly.<br /> <br /> Second, lack of organization with staff wasn't either a uniform thing or unique to them.<br /> <br /> But it has nothing to do with the myth of the ninja anyway. The myth was born in the era of the Shogunate, decades after the end of the Sengoku, in the theater.<br /> <br /> It's a mix of stories about the Jizamurai of Iga and K\u014dku during a particular period, freeform reading of both old and forged shinobi guides, and theater practices and tropes.<br /> <br /> No further ninja attacks were ascribed to the period, and this is exactly the era when the samurai get to be the elite class we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:53:27-07:00","id":1561312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561311#post1561311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No further ninja attacks were ascribed to the period, and this is exactly the era when the samurai get to be the elite class we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, the samurai were not always warriors. They were <i>&quot;ones who serve the nobility&quot;</i> and included a variety of roles. Including, but probably not limited to, accountants and butlers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fun Fact:</b> the last man to hold the position of samurai before they were abolished was a white, western European. So at least the movie was historically accurate in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T16:49:34-07:00","id":1561326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561311#post1561311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how it worked.<br /> <br /> First, Samurai didn't look servants in the eye, which is not the same as not recognizing them despite not staring the face directly.<br /> <br /> Second, lack of organization with staff wasn't either a uniform thing or unique to them.<br /> <br /> But it has nothing to do with the myth of the ninja anyway. The myth was born in the era of the Shogunate, decades after the end of the Sengoku, in the theater.<br /> <br /> It's a mix of stories about the Jizamurai of Iga and K\u014dku during a particular period, freeform reading of both old and forged shinobi guides, and theater practices and tropes.<br /> <br /> No further ninja attacks were ascribed to the period, and this is exactly the era when the samurai get to be the elite class we know.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm well aware of how the &quot;Rappa&quot;(comandos in our terms) got shaped into Ninjas by Japanese theatrical conventions. I've read more than one book on the subject. One of the books illustrated aspects of the transformation with exquisite prints in incredibly rich colors. It was in a book written by a Japanese scholar of 17th century Japanese social and artistic history that I encountered the details of how Samurai snobery made assassinations easier. As I am several hundred miles away from the university library where I read the books I can't get the titles or authors for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-04-2026, 07:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T19:39:01-07:00","id":1561329,"title":"","content":"Also, katanas are pretty mid tier, if not outright shit weapons. Their status as the god of all swords is mostly due to pop culture media and western propaganda.<br /> <br /> Folding the metal a thousand times would actually damage its integrity, and they are far from being the first / only curved blades in the world.<br /> <br /> You'd be far better off using a European sword, than a Japanese one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T19:52:52-07:00","id":1561331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561329#post1561329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, katanas are pretty mid tier, if not outright shit weapons. Their status as the god of all swords is mostly due to pop culture media and western propaganda.<br /> <br /> Folding the metal a thousand times would actually damage its integrity, and they are far from being the first / only curved blades in the world.<br /> <br /> You'd be far better off using a European sword, than a Japanese one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. But the skill involved in making a katana is and impressive feat of metallurgy. The available iron was of such low quality that it took amazing skill to forge even a mainly viable sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T20:13:05-07:00","id":1561332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561329#post1561329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, katanas are pretty mid tier, if not outright shit weapons. Their status as the god of all swords is mostly due to pop culture media and western propaganda.<br /> <br /> Folding the metal a thousand times would actually damage its integrity, and they are far from being the first / only curved blades in the world.<br /> <br /> You'd be far better off using a European sword, than a Japanese one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's heavily overcorrecting.<br /> <br /> Katanas are good swords at what they do, and what they do is lethal in the context they were used.<br /> <br /> Could they be better? Maybe. But not at all a bad overall design.<br /> <br /> Actual swords of any type, though, vary hugely from piece to piece. There are exceptional swords and shitty swords everywhere. Most YouTubers that make comparison haven't done any effort at guaranteeing quality.<br /> <br /> Folding the metal would not damage structure, the result would depend more on a lot of other details of the procedure, as the folding is a way to remove impurities and control carbon content. A swordsmith would observe to see when the metal needs one of the many side processes involved.<br /> <br /> Most of their fame is indeed pop culture and propaganda, though not only &quot;western&quot; (which just means US in this case). It began right after the Sengoku as part of a deliberate effort by Tokugawa Iyeyasu to direct the Japanese cultural landscape. He invested heavily in the romanticization of the Sengoku, including the Samurai, the Ninja and the Katana.<br /> <br /> In Japanese, by the way, Katana just means &quot;Japanese Sword&quot;, as in opposed to Chinese style swords they used before. The name refer to a huge category of swords. What we usually call a katana is an Uchigatana.<br /> <br /> You're not &quot;far better off&quot; using an European sword. You're better off using whatever fits your training and technique (another thing some YouTubers do not acknowledge).<br /> <br /> For war, you're also better off sheeting the sword altogether if you're infantry, as everyone would instead use a spear. Swords are backup.<br /> <br /> On other notes, what Samurai did or not varied greatly through time. Contemporary scholars had contemporary political interests. And the Japanese iron wasn't particularly bad, that's a stupid legend. All iron ore at the time was mostly bad and each place developed distinct ways to deal with it. A well made Katana or a well made sword from anywhere had excellent steel after the respective correction processes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T09:40:54-07:00","id":1561346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561332#post1561332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's heavily overcorrecting.<br /> <br /> Katanas are good swords at what they do, and what they do is lethal in the context they were used.<br /> <br /> Could they be better? Maybe. But not at all a bad overall design.<br /> <br /> Actual swords of any type, though, vary hugely from piece to piece. There are exceptional swords and shitty swords everywhere. Most YouTubers that make comparison haven't done any effort at guaranteeing quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I could remember the video I heard this quote from, but: <i>&quot;Japanese steel is shit. Which is why you have to beat the impurities out of it, like a local Vicar!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I don't doubt that the design itself might be good for its intended purpose. But the materials used in their creation failed to live up to the hype surrounding them.<br /> <br /> Modern technology and forging methods have probably corrected this issue, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T16:50:43-07:00","id":1561357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561346#post1561346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish I could remember the video I heard this quote from, but: <i>&quot;Japanese steel is shit. Which is why you have to beat the impurities out of it, like a local Vicar!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I don't doubt that the design itself might be good for its intended purpose. But the materials used in their creation failed to live up to the hype surrounding them.<br /> <br /> Modern technology and forging methods have probably corrected this issue, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just said YouTube videos shouldn't be trusted by default, they frequently replicate a lot of myths. And there are myths on both sides. I've seen lots of videos saying all kinds of things or doing all kinds of incorrect tests, and read a lot of actual historical research on the matter.<br /> <br /> Japanese steel isn't shit, but Japanese iron sources were full of impurities. And so was the ore taken from bogs in Europe at the time. The metal workers on both places had to develop purification processes, or the result would be in both cases a useless piece of slag.<br /> <br /> Europeans did it with their furnace technology, but even then the process was complicated and demanded constant supervision and course correction. Japanese did during blade crafting instead, with similar sofistication.<br /> <br /> Both still got a lot of quality variation because the end result was a lot of rubbish metal and progressive rarity as you reach top tier swords for the richest nobility. You got far more quality variation between a cheap sword and a masterpiece than you would get comparing entirely distinct sword crafting technology, as long as it reached the same material.<br /> <br /> So the materials were pretty good on both, not due to pure sources in either, but because both had the means to correct it. And modern tech can extract and purify steel with any source. In fact, you can purify Japanese sand iron with a magnet, though it's not the best method.<br /> <br /> The material wouldn't live to the hype because the hype is bullshit, but so is the hype on European swords or the notion that Japanese ones were bad. They weren't.<br /> <br /> What changes with design is the kind of technique you use and the combat situations where each shines most.<br /> <br /> And one thing the katana does better: it cuts better in most situations, not because of material or sharpness, but because the curved blade makes easier to execute a straight cut, which is not a marginal advantage in war, when you can't have only super masters, you need a soldier to be battle-ready in few months.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T17:04:27-07:00","id":1561359,"title":"","content":"Japan has long been advanced in metallurgy. It's one of the reasons the English couldn't get a market in 16th century Japan. The two nations were on a par in metallurgy. Each could have taught the other a great deal, but they were roughly equals in metallurgy.<br /> <br /> Japanese iron ore forced the Japanese blacksmiths to develop impressive skill. However, there were other highly skilled blacksmiths working with better ore. Take the swordsmiths of Damascus. There are reasons they spoke about Damascus steel well into the 19th century.<br /> <br /> Sure, katanas represent an impressive achievement. The best swords made of Damascus steel were substantially better. That reflects local materials not technological limitations in Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T17:22:28-07:00","id":1561362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561359#post1561359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Japan has long been advanced in metallurgy. It's one of the reasons the English couldn't get a market in 16th century Japan. The two nations were on a par in metallurgy. Each could have taught the other a great deal, but they were roughly equals in metallurgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was because of xenophobia, with the Japanese government opting to close their borders to foreigners?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> I'm not aware of any particular hype surrounding European swords. It seems to be the opposite, with people thinking that the blades were ineffective, because you could safely grab them with your hand.<br /> <br /> However, this overlooks the fact that as long as the blade wasn't being actively dragged across your flesh, simply clutching it wasn't all that dangerous. Especially if you're wearing gloves at the time. You could also use the hand guard like a pickaxe, by swinging at the gaps and soft points in the enemy's armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T18:10:39-07:00","id":1561365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561359#post1561359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Japan has long been advanced in metallurgy. It's one of the reasons the English couldn't get a market in 16th century Japan. The two nations were on a par in metallurgy. Each could have taught the other a great deal, but they were roughly equals in metallurgy.<br /> <br /> Japanese iron ore forced the Japanese blacksmiths to develop impressive skill. However, there were other highly skilled blacksmiths working with better ore. Take the swordsmiths of Damascus. There are reasons they spoke about Damascus steel well into the 19th century.<br /> <br /> Sure, katanas represent an impressive achievement. The best swords made of Damascus steel were substantially better. That reflects local materials not technological limitations in Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another legend.<br /> <br /> Damascus steel was impressive in the 19th century because they had perfectly preserved old swords and thought this was due to the steel, but was due to how they were preserved.<br /> <br /> Most &quot;popular knowledge&quot; about swords come from 19th century experts that didn't thought that some past swords were just for show and didn't need high quality. The idea that swords were dull or heavy, for example, comes from the fact most surviving medieval swords survived precisely because they were to hang on a wall or something and never saw battle.<br /> <br /> This ties directly in the hype around the katana: it started because US soldiers that fought in Japan in WWII got some swords from defeated officials and noticed the stark superiority from the sabers used by US officials. But the reality: US officials, like anywhere else but Japan at the time, got ceremonial swords never meant for real use. Japanese officials had a tradition of requesting real, battle-ready swords.<br /> <br /> There were no significantly better ore before modern metallurgy. And wouldn't make much of a difference, it would just make the purifying process easier. The final result in all cases was scarily close to modern steel in good swords. It's just that now we manage superlative purity in bulk and at a low cost.<br /> <br /> What Damascus steel has that is impressive is the patterns in the steel that are very beautiful and cool, and we still don't know how they did it. We can replicate a close semblance, but by other methods they wouldn't have. It's just cool to look, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561362#post1561362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was because of xenophobia, with the Japanese government opting to close their borders to foreigners?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither.<br /> <br /> Japan closed the borders for a series of social, strategic and economic reasons. And it wasn't a full closure: they retained contact with the Dutch and commerce was still intense, but with heavy controls and foreigners consigned to the port of Nagasaki.<br /> <br /> Basically Europe was already starting colonial processes through Asia and the Shogunate saw it. Problems compounded: Christianity had the risk of drifting people's loyalty from country to the papacy, which was a legit threat at the time, local lords could still use foreigners to amass power against the still stabilizing shogunate, and European style commerce was a real risk to metal reserves. Yes, the European actually wanted Japanese metal.<br /> <br /> Add a pinch of popular demand: Christian communities in Japan sometimes engaged in vandalism and destruction against local sacred places and objects, so that had to be contained too.<br /> <br /> On hype, the video you saw is precisely a part of it. With the growth of HEMA, there has been a growing hype over European swords that stay &quot;subtle&quot; by making bad comparisons and avoid the most ludicrous claims, so they appear more balanced when they're not.<br /> <br /> And yes, you can hold a sword's blade, that's by the way the basis of some techniques. Katanas aren't meant for this exactly, although they also could be held by the blade in some contexts. It is not completely correct that you had to drag the sword, but it was not lack of sharpness, but just right technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T20:49:46-07:00","id":1561367,"title":"","content":"This thread started as a funny idea for an Akashic Rote, and has since become educational. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T23:19:47-07:00","id":1561369,"title":"","content":"Various iron ores have different impurities. This affects the quality of the metal made from that ore unless you have quality metallurgy to purify the ore. One of the reasons the Titanic sank is the high acidity of the Iron Ore the ship's steel plates were made of. <br /> <br /> Japan, until modern times had no access to high quality iron ore. They made do. Sure there are impressive qualities to katanas. Katanas also are fragile in several ways western and South Asian swords aren't. These qualities were a blend of consequences from the qualities of the original iron ore and the consequences of the special qualities of the blade. Example, katanas need to be kept clearer than other swords or they rust badly. The treatments that create an extra sharp edge made points less practical. Trade offs.<br /> <br /> Now Monteparnas will say I'm horribly wrong and scold me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T00:09:09-07:00","id":1561371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561369#post1561369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now Monteparnas will say I'm horribly wrong and scold me.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'll say you're wrong on some parts and lecture everyone because I'm almost physically incapable of containing myself. And I sincerely apologize if I'm being too offensive, I'll try to moderate myself if that's the case.<br /> <br /> You are right that ore quality matters if you don't have high quality metallurgy to purify it. But the point is that swordsmith tech did that exactly. Without this the steel simply wouldn't be capable of making a useful blade, it would be too brittle. There are uses for lesser steel, but blades need high grade, period.<br /> <br /> Even then there was a lot of variability. If we compare high quality swords made for nobles, royalty, or even rich merchants, we're talking near-modern steel. But if we talk the swords of regular soldiers, there's a lot of bad swords.<br /> <br /> But the point is, that was true on both cases, because Europeans at the time used bog iron, which isn't any better than Japanese sand iron, it's maybe a little worse. The mines with good ore would be explored later. So both were using bad ore, but also both were purifying it very well when it came to making good swords.<br /> <br /> You are right that there are tradeoffs. That's basically my point this whole time. The idea that one type of sword was intrinsically superior is plain wrong, but they didn't work the same way.<br /> <br /> And yes, katanas rust easier. This is not an old problem linked to ore quality, though, this is a general problem because they specifically require steel with greater carbon content, which rusts more easily. This is a requirement for the exact rigidity it needs to be used the way it is, and this carbon was actually added in the forging process, not an ore impurity.<br /> <br /> European swords are also a far greater variety of swords than it seems. Katanas too, but not nearly as much. But most European swords, and certainly the ones that usually come to mind, are more shaped for thrusting than cut. Katanas are bad at thrust, though it was also used, just far less.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, none live up to the hype of swords in general as a concept. They're good weapons, but hardly the best or most used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T00:27:15-07:00","id":1561372,"title":"","content":"Not gonna lie, the term &quot;Bog Iron&quot; sounds like it came straight from a fantasy novel.<br /> <br /> While using a magnet to draw metal particles out of sand and forge them into weapons is definitely something you'd see in a battle anime.<br /> <br /> But yeah, thrusting weapons would have been more practical. Because contrary to what popular media has conditioned us to believe, armor is actually effective at protecting you!<br /> <br /> Chopping through a suit of metal armor, with a padded gambeson for reinforcement underneath, would have been rather difficult for most people.<br /> <br /> Which, upon retrospect, is probably why ancient leaders felt confident enough to ride into battle ahead of their armies, instead of sitting behind a command desk these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T01:23:22-07:00","id":1561375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561372#post1561372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not gonna lie, the term &quot;Bog Iron&quot; sounds like it came straight from a fantasy novel.<br /> <br /> While using a magnet to draw metal particles out of sand and forge them into weapons is definitely something you'd see in a battle anime.<br /> <br /> But yeah, thrusting weapons would have been more practical. Because contrary to what popular media has conditioned us to believe, armor is actually effective at protecting you!<br /> <br /> Chopping through a suit of metal armor, with a padded gambeson for reinforcement underneath, would have been rather difficult for most people.<br /> <br /> Which, upon retrospect, is probably why ancient leaders felt confident enough to ride into battle ahead of their armies, instead of sitting behind a command desk these days.</div> </div> </div> </div>About bog iron, I thought the same first time I heard it.<br /> <br /> On armor, chopping through metal wasn't hard, it simply wasn't a thing. You could have the strength, the sword wouldn't. That said a lot of variables could affect how you could hurt your target, that's not it.<br /> <br /> Spears have reach and are easy to use, they can control area better and are easy to use in formation. They have a lot of advantages for battlefields. Swords were side weapons due to their versatility, both as tools and weapons that worked with great variety of techniques. You'd be better off with a sword on daily life, not because it was the best weapon in any particular situation, but because it would be useful at most situations.<br /> <br /> Now we do with combat knives, since we don't need all the reach of a sword anymore. And we keep turning rifles into spears with bayonets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T13:29:14-07:00","id":1561429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560092-beating-common-sense-into-people?p=1561367#post1561367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread started as a funny idea for an Akashic Rote, and has since become educational. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's always time to circle back to it. It could function like how Secret Arts in Weapons of the Gods establish superior wisdom through superior kung fu - if the advisor just beat you soundly in a duel, maybe what you were planning on was, in fact, a bad idea, and you should stop before you hurt yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}